When it comes to enjoying a fine whiskey, the container is not merely a vessel; it is a tool for professional evaluation. To truly appreciate the nuances of a Speyside malt or a high-rye bourbon, one must consider the physics of aroma.

### The Glencairn: The Gold Standard
The tulip-shaped Glencairn is widely considered the essential glass for any enthusiast. Its tapered mouth concentrates the vapors, directing the "nose" toward the olfactory senses while allowing the heavier ethanol to dissipate.

> "Whiskey is 90% aroma. Without the right glass, you are missing 90% of the experience."

### The Traditional Rocks Glass
While the "Old Fashioned" or "Rocks" glass is a staple of cinema and lounges, its wide rim is designed for cocktails and ice rather than neat sipping. It is the glass of choice for social drinking, where the aesthetic of the heavy crystal base provides a satisfying tactile experience.

### Final Thoughts
If you are tasting a new bottle for the first time, reach for the Glencairn. If you are sitting by a fire with a trusted favorite and a single large cube, the weighted rocks glass is your best companion.